WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.552
- Does anyone else with a sibling

00:00:01.552 --> 00:00:03.973
with a disability have
this conversation a lot?

00:00:03.973 --> 00:00:08.015
- Sheena, how can I find
someone to go on a date with?

00:00:08.015 --> 00:00:10.744
- Wait, I should start from the beginning.

00:00:10.744 --> 00:00:13.029
This is me and my little brother Sean.

00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:15.531
Ever since he came
along, he was my best bud

00:00:15.531 --> 00:00:18.589
and I just wanted to take care of him.

00:00:18.589 --> 00:00:19.907
Before he turned one, we found out

00:00:19.907 --> 00:00:22.681
that he had cerebral palsy, but to me

00:00:22.681 --> 00:00:24.205
he was always just Sean.

00:00:24.205 --> 00:00:26.613
So we were like any
other pair of siblings.

00:00:26.613 --> 00:00:29.018
And for a while there
really got at each other.

00:00:29.018 --> 00:00:29.851
(click)

00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:32.485
But I swear, now we get along much better.

00:00:32.485 --> 00:00:34.936
So my brother has cerebral palsy and a lot

00:00:34.936 --> 00:00:37.236
of things in life are a little
more challenging for him.

00:00:37.236 --> 00:00:38.892
One of those things is dating

00:00:38.892 --> 00:00:41.538
but I decided I'm going
to sit down and talk

00:00:41.538 --> 00:00:45.044
to him about dating and then
I'm going to find him a date.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:47.035
(electronic beats)

00:00:47.035 --> 00:00:49.939
So first I asked him, why is
it important for him to date?

00:00:49.939 --> 00:00:51.272
- I feel lonely.

00:00:52.136 --> 00:00:55.032
I want to be with someone.

00:00:55.032 --> 00:00:57.798
I try my best and asking my friends

00:00:57.798 --> 00:01:01.131
like if they want to go on coffee dates.

00:01:02.308 --> 00:01:03.736
- Mhm.

00:01:03.736 --> 00:01:05.853
It's hard to know who to ask out.

00:01:05.853 --> 00:01:07.486
And when you just have things

00:01:07.486 --> 00:01:08.972
in common and when you're just friends

00:01:08.972 --> 00:01:10.924
and when it's a genuine
connection that could turn

00:01:10.924 --> 00:01:13.204
into something more romantic.

00:01:13.204 --> 00:01:15.507
But I feel like it's easier

00:01:15.507 --> 00:01:18.924
for people who have no disability at all.

00:01:20.221 --> 00:01:21.715
Like you, for example.

00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:26.210
Me, I try and asking my
crush in middle school.

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:28.594
It was the junior-senior dance.

00:01:28.594 --> 00:01:30.256
She stood me up.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:33.391
I think that's hard for me to find someone

00:01:33.391 --> 00:01:35.224
because my disability.

00:01:36.658 --> 00:01:39.766
People just look at me weird.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.683
My walking, my talking.

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:45.976
I feel like they say,

00:01:45.976 --> 00:01:49.139
"I don't like, I don't
want to go out with that."

00:01:49.139 --> 00:01:51.889
I just wish people more flexible.

00:01:53.806 --> 00:01:56.208
- So what kind of stuff
would you want to do

00:01:56.208 --> 00:01:57.480
if you got a girlfriend?

00:01:57.480 --> 00:02:00.484
(electronic beats)

00:02:00.484 --> 00:02:03.878
- I would want to do hand gliding.

00:02:03.878 --> 00:02:04.953
(laughing)

00:02:04.953 --> 00:02:07.794
- I'm talking about just
like everyday stuff.

00:02:07.794 --> 00:02:08.627
- Okay.

00:02:08.627 --> 00:02:11.543
Stuff like going on the
treadmill, working out.

00:02:11.543 --> 00:02:13.350
- You guys are both going
to be on one treadmill

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:14.480
at the same time?

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.313
- Yeah

00:02:15.313 --> 00:02:17.705
Singing, playing video games.

00:02:17.705 --> 00:02:20.788
Playing board games, watching movies.

00:02:22.359 --> 00:02:23.595
Going out.

00:02:23.595 --> 00:02:25.147
- Other than the treadmill part,

00:02:25.147 --> 00:02:27.357
all those sound like
really fun date ideas.

00:02:27.357 --> 00:02:28.190
- Yeah.

00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.963
- How about we find you a date?

00:02:29.963 --> 00:02:30.796
- Yay.

00:02:30.796 --> 00:02:32.147
- Since we are in the time of COVID,

00:02:32.147 --> 00:02:33.013
we are going to be looking

00:02:33.013 --> 00:02:34.597
for a virtual date, right?

00:02:34.597 --> 00:02:35.949
And I will be using the power

00:02:35.949 --> 00:02:38.242
of the internet to find this lady.

00:02:38.242 --> 00:02:41.314
So I'm going to take a few
notes on what we are looking for

00:02:41.314 --> 00:02:44.946
and what you want to share about yourself.

00:02:44.946 --> 00:02:47.989
So how would you describe yourself?

00:02:47.989 --> 00:02:50.572
- Funny, creative and outgoing.

00:02:52.088 --> 00:02:53.505
- Yes. Very true.

00:02:54.578 --> 00:02:56.330
What is something else
that you want people

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.414
to know about you?

00:02:57.414 --> 00:02:59.250
- My shirt business.

00:02:59.250 --> 00:03:00.477
- Of course.

00:03:00.477 --> 00:03:01.310
Should we show people?

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.143
- Yeah.

00:03:02.143 --> 00:03:02.976
- Let's see your shirt.

00:03:02.976 --> 00:03:05.217
- Ta-da!
- All right.

00:03:05.217 --> 00:03:07.259
So this is ink man.
- Yeah.

00:03:07.259 --> 00:03:10.476
- And you have a few different
designs that you've drawn?

00:03:10.476 --> 00:03:11.309
(popping)

00:03:11.309 --> 00:03:12.851
And where did these come from?

00:03:12.851 --> 00:03:14.418
These characters?

00:03:14.418 --> 00:03:16.166
- I just thought of them.

00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:17.616
My imagination.

00:03:17.616 --> 00:03:20.354
- And where can we find
your art and your t-shirts?

00:03:20.354 --> 00:03:22.109
- On my Instagram page.

00:03:22.109 --> 00:03:24.574
- I think I have enough
information now to scour the web

00:03:24.574 --> 00:03:26.535
and see if I can find a lovely lady

00:03:26.535 --> 00:03:28.996
for you to go on a virtual date with.

00:03:28.996 --> 00:03:29.829
- Awesome.

00:03:29.829 --> 00:03:30.662
- Awesome.

00:03:30.662 --> 00:03:31.495
(sentimental piano music)

00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:33.523
Sean has been wanting
a girlfriend for ages.

00:03:33.523 --> 00:03:35.579
Like he has been talking
about wanting to go

00:03:35.579 --> 00:03:38.043
on dates and meet someone for so long.

00:03:38.043 --> 00:03:40.361
He just wants to experience romance

00:03:40.361 --> 00:03:43.111
and love and not unrequited love.

00:03:44.396 --> 00:03:47.569
We all just want to be
loved and to love, right?

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:50.342
And I sure hope he finds that one day.

00:03:50.342 --> 00:03:53.430
And in the meantime, I'm going
to do what I can to help.

00:03:53.430 --> 00:03:54.263
Okay, Sean.

00:03:54.263 --> 00:03:56.496
I have found a few lovely
ladies who are interested

00:03:56.496 --> 00:03:59.140
in going on a virtual date with
you and we're going to look

00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.022
through them and you're
going to choose one.

00:04:01.022 --> 00:04:01.855
- Okay.

00:04:01.855 --> 00:04:02.688
- Okay.

00:04:02.688 --> 00:04:03.675
Option number one, she's looking

00:04:03.675 --> 00:04:05.230
for a long-term relationship

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:07.487
with someone who she can
be comfortable around

00:04:07.487 --> 00:04:10.686
who is her best friend, and
they can have fun together.

00:04:10.686 --> 00:04:15.686
And number two, she plays the
keyboard, plays video games.

00:04:16.109 --> 00:04:18.664
Likes to go on hikes.

00:04:18.664 --> 00:04:20.768
This is our final option.

00:04:20.768 --> 00:04:22.427
She is looking for a man who is kind

00:04:22.427 --> 00:04:24.568
and is able to get her
out of her shell a bit.

00:04:24.568 --> 00:04:26.946
She loves movies and going to concerts.

00:04:26.946 --> 00:04:28.519
Want to see more about her?

00:04:28.519 --> 00:04:29.352
- Yeah.

00:04:29.352 --> 00:04:30.897
- Hi, I'm Melissa.

00:04:30.897 --> 00:04:33.773
I live outside of Pittsburgh, PA

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:37.856
and my hobbies are I like
reading and watching TV

00:04:40.198 --> 00:04:41.781
and jigsaw puzzles.

00:04:43.045 --> 00:04:43.878
- Yeah.

00:04:43.878 --> 00:04:44.711
- Is she your winner?

00:04:44.711 --> 00:04:45.544
- Yeah.

00:04:45.544 --> 00:04:46.377
- Yeah?

00:04:46.377 --> 00:04:47.210
- Yes.

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.043
- All right.

00:04:48.043 --> 00:04:52.069
We will be setting you up
on a date with Melissa.

00:04:52.069 --> 00:04:52.902
- Yay.

00:04:54.569 --> 00:04:56.926
- [Sheena] Hey bud, you
excited for your date today?

00:04:56.926 --> 00:04:57.759
- Yeah.

00:04:57.759 --> 00:04:59.531
- [Sheena] Then let's get ready.

00:04:59.531 --> 00:05:00.541
- Hi.

00:05:00.541 --> 00:05:02.458
- Hi, nice to meet you.

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:04.635
How are you?

00:05:07.032 --> 00:05:08.406
- Oh I'm good, how are you?

00:05:08.406 --> 00:05:09.823
- Good.

00:05:09.823 --> 00:05:11.486
- Okay, I'm sitting in the other room

00:05:11.486 --> 00:05:14.539
and I'm so nervous for him.

00:05:14.539 --> 00:05:18.050
She seems very high functioning
and maybe even neuro-typical

00:05:18.050 --> 00:05:20.457
with just some physical disabilities.

00:05:20.457 --> 00:05:23.443
And that's something that's
really interesting about CP is

00:05:23.443 --> 00:05:27.120
that CP is a very kind of umbrella term,

00:05:27.120 --> 00:05:30.333
where there are a lot of variations

00:05:30.333 --> 00:05:32.411
in what CP can look like.

00:05:32.411 --> 00:05:34.128
So some people just have a little bit

00:05:34.128 --> 00:05:37.645
of a waddle in their walk
and some muscle weakness

00:05:37.645 --> 00:05:39.893
but they're totally neuro-typical.

00:05:39.893 --> 00:05:42.813
Some people are very severely disabled

00:05:42.813 --> 00:05:47.296
and need 24/7 care and can't
really do much on their own.

00:05:47.296 --> 00:05:50.556
So Sean falls kind of in
the middle of everything.

00:05:50.556 --> 00:05:53.198
And that's why he can
be so tricky, I think,

00:05:53.198 --> 00:05:55.611
when it comes to dating
and finding a partner

00:05:55.611 --> 00:05:59.611
because a lot of the people
he knows kind of fall

00:05:59.611 --> 00:06:01.765
on either one end or the other.

00:06:01.765 --> 00:06:03.284
He just needs to find someone

00:06:03.284 --> 00:06:04.926
that will love him for who he is.

00:06:04.926 --> 00:06:07.000
And it's not about the disability, right?

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.485
It's just about finding
someone who intellectually

00:06:09.485 --> 00:06:11.934
can match him in a fun way.

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:13.650
We'll see how this goes.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:14.958
How did it go?

00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:16.791
- It went really well,

00:06:19.218 --> 00:06:21.635
but I want to keep as friends

00:06:22.513 --> 00:06:25.483
because she lives too far away.

00:06:25.483 --> 00:06:28.066
And I don't want to move there.

00:06:29.944 --> 00:06:30.777
- [Sheena] Yeah. That makes sense.

00:06:30.777 --> 00:06:32.384
Well, I'm glad you had fun though.

00:06:32.384 --> 00:06:33.626
And it sounds like you made a new friend.

00:06:33.626 --> 00:06:34.968
- Yay.

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:39.280
I'm so excited to see
who else is out there.

00:06:39.280 --> 00:06:41.879
And I want to keep on dating.

00:06:41.879 --> 00:06:43.689
- So ladies, if he's your type

00:06:43.689 --> 00:06:46.260
I am still down to match-make.

00:06:46.260 --> 00:06:47.093
So hit us up.

00:06:47.093 --> 00:06:51.367
Also, if anyone else knows
other ways to meet people

00:06:51.367 --> 00:06:52.701
for people like Sean,

00:06:52.701 --> 00:06:54.061
let us know.

00:06:54.061 --> 00:06:57.144
(happy guitar music)

